            <ArticleTitle>Recent advances in nuclear cardiology. 1. &quot;Hot-spot&quot; and &quot;cold-spot&quot; myocardial scintigraphy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nuclear cardiology is a comparatively new field of cardiovascular medicine in which technologic advances have provided relatively noninvasive means of evaluating cardiovascular abnormalities. The purpose of this two-part review is to emphasize some important recent advances and to place in perspective the advantages and disadvantages of those new techniques that are particularly useful clinically.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
